Deployment
We deployed the AUV at the shore of Baby Beach in Dana Point, California, to keep the vehicle easy to recover and minimize any environmental impact. A previous lake deployment nearly lost a piece of the vehicle, so staying close to shore was deliberate. We also checked the onboard circuitry before and after the run.
Each run went like this:

Insert an SD card into the motherboard and flip the power switch.
Close the circuitry into its harnessed box and strap it to the AUV.
Let the motors drive the AUV forward until the FSR feels a high enough force (the extrusion pressed against a team member), then back off and repeat.
Retrieve the AUV, then read the SD card log in MATLAB with logreader.m to plot each sensor’s raw voltage. Wind speed was also watched live in the Arduino Serial Monitor.







